@startuml dispatch-lifecycle
title M-DP1: trusted-agent ordinary allocation and one-shot lifecycle (draft; §5.3 intake gate)
participant "Caller process\ncaller UID / principal + key" as C
participant "Dispatcher core\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Dispatcher-owned state\ninputs, records, effects, claims, journal, logs" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; owns account ledger / stop evidence" as H
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; owns binding / lease / grant state" as B
participant "Supervisor\nservice UID; daemon-owned" as S
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot; writes start receipt" as L
participant "curator-run -> harness\nagent UID; agent home / working directory" as E
== prepare and provision (§5.1) ==
C -> C : compose plan, exec-profile reference and resolved PATH; digest
note right of C
  Orchestrator caller: own agent account and Curator home configuration (§5.2).
  Child profile/environment access and narrowed-grant constraints are open (§16).
end note
D -> J : establish controls; classify/account for forward readiness (§7.1)
C -> D : dispatch/1 signed provision or dispatch; caller-scoped root R
D -> J : local lock: snapshot/intent + per-record marker; unlock for reconciliation calls (§4.1)
D -> D : principal/key/signature/chains, quotas, constructibility, digest\nrecord class; require qualified host matrix and exec profile\ntrusted provider-only binding; check caller text; pin ref/digest
D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context prepare
B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + revocation sequence
alt prepare refused, revoked or unavailable
  break prepare refusal
    D --> C : typed refusal; no external effect
  end
else prepare accepted
  D -> J : write immutable input/1
  alt temporary capacity closure
    alt initial slice
      break capacity refusal
        D --> C : capacity:*; no provisioning/start
      end
    else later queue capability
      D -> J : durable bounded fair queue
      D --> C : queued handle
      ... gate opens ...
      D -> D : recheck principal, authority/window, quota and all gates
      D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context dequeue
      B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + sequence
      alt permanent refusal, expired window, revoked or unavailable
        break dequeue refused
          D --> C : refusal (never queue authority/quota failures)
        end
      else capacity still closed
        break remain queued
          D -> J : keep queued; no provisioning/start
        end
      end
    end
  end
  D -> J : owned capacity claim; journal E-create intent
  D -> H : user.create {request_id: E-create, kind: agent}
  alt create observation unknown / contradictory
    break reconcile before further effects
      D -> J : provisioning pending; effect.observe E-create / operation / canonical digest; never automatic new create
    end
  else account created
    H --> D : uid, generation
  else create refused
    break provisioning failure
      D -> J : retiring; confirm applicable cleanup before failed
    end
  end
  opt helper v1
    D -> H : fw.apply admitted pin; served-policy digest check; drift refuses\nits own journaled effect; no state lock held
  end
  D -> D : leaf agent:generation = request intersect caller intersect own grant
  D -> J : E-bind intent; caller chain + intersection dependency
  D -> B : bind {request_id: E-bind, uid, generation, both chains}
  alt bind confirmed
    B --> D : binding_id
    D -> J : allocation idle
  else bind refused or result ambiguous
    break recover failed / uncertain provisioning
      D -> J : known refusal -> retiring; unknown -> observe by E-bind first
      note over D,B
        R-OUTCOME: unfinished admitted bind stays pending; authority-creating retry is fresh.
        Effect absence never authorizes a new bind (§7.1).
        No automatic new effect; standing failures stay pending for operator decision.
        Unbind if bound, retire if created, each confirmed before failed (§5.1).
        Unknown is never treated as absent (§4.6).
      end note
    end
  end
end
== start (§5.3): only an admitted idle owned allocation ==
C -> D : start with separate root R-start (dispatch keeps R)
D -> D : recheck authority / lifetime; capacity claim (initial refusal / later gated queue)
note over D,J
  This figure starts ordinary executions: default 4 h, maximum 12 h.
  Record runtime deadline; sweep stops ordinary executions at that deadline (§7.2).
  Standing start is separate: max_runtime absent; no runtime quota or deadline.
  A supplied standing max_runtime refuses before launch; code mapping unpublished (§16).
end note
alt busy, expired, unowned or invalid authority
  break start refused
    D --> C : typed refusal; no launch
  end
end
D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context start
B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + revocation sequence
alt revoked / unavailable
  break no start effect
    D --> C : refuse; no launch
  end
end
D -> J : under lock claim {execution_id, epoch}; allocation running
D -> S : start supervisor
S -> J : durable registration/acknowledgement; current daemon-instance epoch on every write
D -> J : journal E-launch intent
alt cancel before launch
  D -> J : serialise cancel with claim; mark absent; never call launcher
else launch initiated
  S -> L : launch.start {request_id: E-launch, generation, execution_id, epoch, executor, plan}
  alt receipt / launcher answer unknown
    S -> J : launching pending; wait for receipt/answer; never relaunch
    opt cancel during unknown launch
      D -> S : cancel; wait for receipt or refusal, then stop
    end
    ... receipt or launcher answer becomes known ...
  end
  alt launcher refuses
    L --> S : refusal
    S -> J : failed stage; confirm absence and applicable cleanup
  else launch accepted
    L -> L : user-manager §7 R-FD3 lifecycle; scrub untrusted inherited FDs first
    L -> L : validate generation / executor / home; retain generation lock and verified executable
    L -> L : stage bounded immutable FD3; root receipt; complete UID/GID transition
    L -> L : release generation lock after completed transition; retain executable until exec
    L -> E : staged immutable read-only FD3; verified executable retained until exec
    note over L,E : Executor receives only 0-2 and FD3; internal handles close at last use/exec and on failure.
    S -> J : start receipt {pid, start_time, boot_id}; running
    E -> E : verify only; prepare agent-home working directory; protected binding
    E -> B : own connection; lease (caller dependency rechecked)
    E -> E : qualified injection; exec harness
    alt exit, explicit stop (cancel), operator action, incident hard stop or ordinary max_runtime deadline
      S -> H : exec.stop {request_id: E-stop, generation, execution_id}\nlatest-receipt fence; TERM/grace/KILL UID + per-user domain; quiet-period absence
    else supervisor known absent
      D -> H : recovery exec.stop with same E-stop; record lost after confirmation
    end
    alt termination observation unknown / contradictory
      break stopping pending
        D -> J : stopping pending; retry E-stop; retain capacity; no cleanup success
      end
    else quiet-period account-wide absence confirmed
      H --> D : confirmed termination receipt
      D -> J : outcome; capacity released after confirmed end/absence
    end
  end
end
== applicable cleanup (§5.4; no success from uncertain observations) ==
opt ordinary kept allocation
  D -> J : allocation idle after execution finish
end
opt ordinary dispatch on-exit, retirement, qualified expiry or failed provisioning
  D -> J : retiring / cleaning; journal E-unbind intent if bound
  opt binding exists
    D -> B : unbind {request_id: E-unbind}
    alt unbind confirmed
      B --> D : confirmation
    else unknown / refused
      break cleanup pending
        D -> J : retain cleanup; retry / observe same E-unbind
      end
    end
  end
  opt account was created
    D -> J : discharge workspace export obligation: recorded export or operator waiver\njournal E-retire intent
    D -> H : user.retire {request_id: E-retire, home: delete}
    note over D,H : Local retirement only; bounded deletion batches stay pending under E-retire until full confirmation.
    alt retirement confirmed
      H --> D : confirmation
    else unknown / refused
      break cleanup pending
        D -> J : retain cleanup; retry / observe same E-retire
      end
    end
  end
  opt keeper active; registration recorded identity as one-shot
    D -> J : separate identity-revocation effect after retirement (§14)
    note over D,J : Keeper API is unspecified in spec §14; standing revocation stays operator-only.
  end
  D -> J : terminal only after applicable effects confirmed; unknown/refused cleanup stays pending
end
note over D,J
  R-LOCK: lock intent/in-flight -> unlock cross-service call -> lock/revalidate result.
  Wait graph: state lock -> local journal/records; unlocked workers -> helper/launcher/broker.
  Cancel before issue prevents call; after issue marks cancel requested, retains claim,
  resolves same effect/receipt then stops. Late stale results never reopen delivery/admission.
  Bounded per-record work leaves unrelated recovery controls reachable.
  R-OUTCOME receiver tables map unfinished admitted work to pending (six R-OBS states).
  Same E-stop/arguments progresses after processes_remain; completed replay never signals.
  R-FATE: user-manager §7 defines exact process fate/affected sets; old writers fenced.
  R-TRANSFER: standalone private repository from caller archive; no backlink.
  Child-UID materialize/export and board-owned exact-candidate path: workspace-transfer.puml.
  R-EXEC/R-VERIFY: no builds/tests here; qualified light checks only, verification off-host.
  R-UNTRUSTED: this trusted binding/harness path never serves an untrusted workplace.
  R-STANDING: host-local loops trusted only; plan surfaces digest-checked on launch/restart/resume.
  R-WATCH: own-allocation freeze + journaled exec.stop; operator phone alert.
  R-ALLSTOP: manual hold/all-execution stop; service parts journal separately, unknown keeps hold.
  Expiry cleanup requires wall expiry + trusted time + boot-inclusive elapsed lifetime.
  Direct operator retirement leaves unconfirmed E-unbind as durable obligation.
  Journal intent before every external effect; persist result/observation (§4).
  E-create, E-bind, E-launch, E-stop, E-unbind, E-retire are distinct;
  retries reuse their ID; root (caller,R) retained only as correlation.
  Standing team lifecycle is bring-up-team.puml (§5.5): no allocation expiry;
  standing executions have no max_runtime quota or deadline; sweep never stops them for runtime.
  no automatic retirement on failure, exit or authority loss.
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Operator records from agent sessions refuse; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Only operator-signed standing retirement/re-creation (§5.4).
  Outcome kind is separate from run state (§4.4 / §8.2).
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#5-lifecycle §5 lifecycle]]
  [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#45-effect-ids-and-the-effect-table §4.5 IDs]] / §6 stop / §7 recovery / §9 capacity
  Broker service UID spelling and exact executor intake schema are unspecified in spec §§3.1, 5.3.
endlegend
@enduml
